  "changes_data": [
    {
      "diff": "@@ -22,17 +22,6 @@ If you or your organization would like to contribute or become a sponsor, please\n \n // The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-* wssalink:2025-02[] {notable}\n-Dissection engine crash.\n-wsbuglink:20509[].\n-cveidlink:2025-5601[].\n-// Fixed in master: 5321308630\n-// Fixed in release-4.4: 29a4f378ab\n-// Fixed in release-4.2: 8c186dbb38\n-// CVSS AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H\n-// CWE-120\n-// * Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-04-25-7554.pcap. wsbuglink:20509[].\n-\n // * wssalink:2025-03[] {notable}\n // Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n // wsbuglink:xxx[].\n@@ -50,14 +39,6 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark grabs your ID at 3 am, goes to Waffle House, and insults people.\n \n-* GRPC: protobuf_json only displays the truncated string value. wsbuglink:20392[].\n-* Trailing octet after IPv4 packet end is not detected or displayed in raw bytes. wsbuglink:20423[].\n-* Wireshark does not correctly decode LIN \"go to sleep\" in TECMP and CMP. wsbuglink:20463[].\n-* Fuzz job crash: fuzz-2025-04-25-7554.pcap. wsbuglink:20509[].\n-* WebSocket per-message compression extentions: fail to decompress server messages (from the 2nd) due to parameter handling. wsbuglink:20531[].\n-* null. wsbuglink:20539[].\n-* The LL_PERIODIC_SYNC_WR_IND packet is not properly dissected (packet-btle.c) wsbuglink:20554[].\n-\n === New and Updated Features\n \n There are no new or updated features in this release.\n@@ -77,18 +58,6 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.2.12.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-ASAM CMP\n-F1AP\n-LIN\n-Logcat Text\n-genl\n-net_dm\n-netfilter\n-nvme\n-ProtoBuf\n-Quake\n-TECMP\n-WebSocket\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n@@ -118,6 +87,7 @@ There is no updated file format support in this release.\n This document only describes the changes introduced in Wireshark {wireshark-version}.\n You can find release notes for prior versions at the following locations:\n \n+* https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.12.html[Wireshark 4.2.12]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.11.html[Wireshark 4.2.11]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.10.html[Wireshark 4.2.10]\n * https://www.wireshark.org/docs/relnotes/wireshark-4.2.9.html[Wireshark 4.2.9]\n",
